Rows whose class includes ''LEAD'' block byte movement until their payload and owning principal are proved. Current `face` and `bundle` fields describe filename/export selection only (`vault-carriers.ts:119-165`); they never confer cryptographic separation. The existing VK rotation sweeps all hot/cold rows (`:64-68,477-510`), so K15 replaces it with per-face and named-S rotation.

